 Vitamin A, Vitamin C, and Manganese. It is also considered a good source of protein.<br\/>","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#faq-question-1661691506361","position":2,"url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#faq-question-1661691506361","name":"Can you freeze the leftovers?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, the leftovers can be frozen and kept in the freezer for up to 3 months. Make sure you cool them down totally and wrap them individually before freezing them.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#faq-question-1661691545245","position":3,"url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#faq-question-1661691545245","name":"Can you prepare lahmacun in advance?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can make the mince filling up to 3 days in advance and keep it refrigerated in an airtight container until you need it. <br\/>The same goes for the dough. Make sure to bring the dough to room temperature before dividing and rolling them out.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Recipe","name":"Turkish Lahmacun","author":{"@id":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/#\/schema\/person\/8cce334b953b929dde2ec84a77dafd5f"},"description":"Homemade Turkish Lahmacun (or Lahmajun-Lahmajoun) is a super-thin crispy flatbread topped with minced beef or lamb mixed with vegetables, herbs, and spices. ","datePublished":"2021-11-01T17:38:40+00:00","image":["https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/11\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-26.jpg","https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/11\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-26-500x500.jpg","https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/11\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-26-500x375.jpg","https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/11\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-26-480x270.jpg"],"video":{"name":"Turkish Lahmacun (Lahmajun)","description":"Homemade Turkish Lahmacun (or Lahmajun-Lahmajoun) is a super-thin crispy flatbread topped with minced beef or lamb mixed with vegetables, herbs, and spices. You can find this popular street \/ fast food everywhere in Turkey, in restaurants, cafes, and fast-food shops.","thumbnailUrl":"https:\/\/content.jwplatform.com\/thumbs\/lojVxLyy-720.jpg","contentUrl":"https:\/\/content.jwplatform.com\/videos\/lojVxLyy.mp4","uploadDate":"2023-01-06T00:00:00+00:00","@type":"VideoObject"},"recipeYield":["6","6 lahmacun"],"prepTime":"PT25M","cookTime":"PT25M","totalTime":"PT50M","recipeIngredient":["2 ¾ cups strong white flour ((330 grams))","¾ cups water + 1 tbsp ((200 ml))","1 tbsp olive oil ((15 ml))","1 TSP salt ((8 grams))","12 ounces ground lamb or beef with %20 fat ((350 grams))","2  tomatoes  ((12 ounces\/300-350 grams))","1 medium onion","2 cloves garlic","2  Turkish green peppers  ((or 1 green bell pepper))","1  red romano pepper  ((or 1 red bell pepper))","1  red chilli ((or ½ TSP chilli flakes))","1 tbsp tomato paste","1 tbsp red pepper paste","1 cup parsley ((finely chopped))","½ TSP freshly ground black pepper","½ TSP paprika","1 ½ TSP salt"],"recipeInstructions":[{"@type":"HowToSection","name":"Preparing the Dough","itemListElement":[{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Place the water, olive oil, and salt in a bowl and mix them until combined. Use a stand mixer if you prefer.","name":"Place the water, olive oil, and salt in a bowl and mix them until combined. Use a stand mixer if you prefer.","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-0-0"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Add the flour gradually and knead the dough. Use the dough hook if you are using your stand mixer. Add enough flour to have the dough come together and form a soft and slightly sticky dough.","name":"Add the flour gradually and knead the dough. Use the dough hook if you are using your stand mixer. Add enough flour to have the dough come together and form a soft and slightly sticky dough.","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-0-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Knead the dough for 5-6 minutes, until it is elastic, smooth, and not sticky anymore.","name":"Knead the dough for 5-6 minutes, until it is elastic, smooth, and not sticky anymore.","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-0-2"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Once the dough is smooth, divide it into 6 balls (approximately 3 oz\/90 grams each) and place them on a lightly floured tray or worktop.","name":"Once the dough is smooth, divide it into 6 balls (approximately 3 oz\/90 grams each) and place them on a lightly floured tray or worktop.","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-0-3"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Cover the dough balls with a clean kitchen towel or cling film and let them rest at room temperature for about 20 minutes. This step is necessary for the dough to relax and makes it easier to roll out. ","name":"Cover the dough balls with a clean kitchen towel or cling film and let them rest at room temperature for about 20 minutes. This step is necessary for the dough to relax and makes it easier to roll out. ","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-0-4"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Prepare lahmacun filling while the dough is resting.","name":"Prepare lahmacun filling while the dough is resting.","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-0-5"}]},{"@type":"HowToSection","name":"Preparing the Filling","itemListElement":[{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Place onion, peppers (both green and red), tomatoes, garlic, and chili (if using fresh) in a food processor and finely chop them using the pulse function. Be careful at this stage not to turn them into pure. Alternatively, finely chop them using a knife.","name":"Place onion, peppers (both green and red), tomatoes, garlic, and chili (if using fresh) in a food processor and finely chop them using the pulse function. Be careful at this stage not to turn them into pure. Alternatively, finely chop them using a knife.","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-1-0"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Transfer the vegetables to a bowl and add the ground meat, tomato paste, pepper paste (you can replace it with tomato paste if you don&#39;t have it in your fridge), finely chopped parsley, freshly ground black pepper, paprika, and salt.","name":"Transfer the vegetables to a bowl and add the ground meat, tomato paste, pepper paste (you can replace it with tomato paste if you don&#39;t have it in your fridge), finely chopped parsley, freshly ground black pepper, paprika, and salt.","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-1-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Mix well until all combined into a smooth mixture that is easy to spread.","name":"Mix well until all combined into a smooth mixture that is easy to spread.","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-1-2"}]},{"@type":"HowToSection","name":"Start Cooking Lahmacun on a Pan","itemListElement":[{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Preheat the oven to 230° C (450° F) and then line a large sheet tray with parchment paper. Set it aside.","name":"Preheat the oven to 230° C (450° F) and then line a large sheet tray with parchment paper. Set it aside.","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-2-0"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Heat a large non-stick pan with a lid over medium-high heat. Ideally, the pan should be 26 cm (10&quot;)Ø or bigger.","name":"Heat a large non-stick pan with a lid over medium-high heat. Ideally, the pan should be 26 cm (10&quot;)Ø or bigger.","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-2-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Roll out a dough ball into a thin circle size of 25 cm (9 ½&quot;) Ø. If your pan is smaller than that, roll the dough ball small enough to fit in it.","name":"Roll out a dough ball into a thin circle size of 25 cm (9 ½&quot;) Ø. If your pan is smaller than that, roll the dough ball small enough to fit in it.","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-2-2"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Gently place the dough circle in the hot pan.","name":"Gently place the dough circle in the hot pan.","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-2-3"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Divide your mixture into 6 and spread ⅙ of the mixture on a dough circle evenly and thinly, including the edges. ","name":"Divide your mixture into 6 and spread ⅙ of the mixture on a dough circle evenly and thinly, including the edges. ","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-2-4"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Gently press on the filling to make sure it sticks to the dough. ","name":"Gently press on the filling to make sure it sticks to the dough. ","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-2-5"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Cook it for 4-5 minutes or until you see some brown spots at the bottom.","name":"Cook it for 4-5 minutes or until you see some brown spots at the bottom.","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-2-6"}]},{"@type":"HowToSection","name":"Finishing Baking in the Oven","itemListElement":[{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Transfer the lahmacun to your prepared baking sheet.","name":"Transfer the lahmacun to your prepared baking sheet.","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-3-0"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Bake them in the preheated oven for 5 to 7 minutes or until they are crispy on the outside and the filling is thoroughly cooked. ","name":"Bake them in the preheated oven for 5 to 7 minutes or until they are crispy on the outside and the filling is thoroughly cooked. ","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-3-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Transfer them to a large plate and then cover them with tin foil or a clean kitchen towel while the rest of the lahmacuns are baking. Covering them will help to keep the lahmacuns warm, and it will soften them enough for you to be able to roll them into wraps.","name":"Transfer them to a large plate and then cover them with tin foil or a clean kitchen towel while the rest of the lahmacuns are baking. Covering them will help to keep the lahmacuns warm, and it will soften them enough for you to be able to roll them into wraps.","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-3-2"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"You can prepare the second dough ball while the first one is baking. Repeat with the remaining dough balls and filling.","name":"You can prepare the second dough ball while the first one is baking. Repeat with the remaining dough balls and filling.","url":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#wprm-recipe-8672-step-3-3"}]}],"aggregateRating":{"@type":"AggregateRating","ratingValue":"5","ratingCount":"21","reviewCount":"15"},"review":[{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Thanks a lot Ayla for the details\r\nIt definitely helps : )","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Laura"},"datePublished":"2022-08-30"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Perfect, good instructions! Good bit of prep but the effort is worth it was top drawer.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Gary"},"datePublished":"2022-06-11"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"My husband loves lamb and raved about the topping on this! Thanks for the recipe.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Katherine"},"datePublished":"2022-05-16"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"It is easy to make and delicious, everyone loves it. Thanks","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Francisco"},"datePublished":"2022-04-27"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"I love the meat mixture! So much flavour!!! This is so perfect and taste great!","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Siri"},"datePublished":"2022-04-24"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"The flavours sound incredible! Such a great make ahead lunch or dinner option!","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Elenora"},"datePublished":"2022-04-16"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Awesome Recipe!\r\nworth the time and effort","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Tommy"},"datePublished":"2022-04-12"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"I am so glad I made this recipe! It was beyond delicious. My husband and I couldn't get enough! We will definitely be making it again!","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Claudia"},"datePublished":"2022-04-11"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"This is my first time seeing a recipe for Turkish Lahmacun, looks fantastic! I love all the flavours and yet it's so simple to make!  I'll be trying this very soon.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Rita"},"datePublished":"2022-04-10"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"We love lahmacun and yours looks tasty. This reminds me I should make it again soon!","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Jasmine"},"datePublished":"2022-04-09"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Just made this tonight and loved it! The kids ate it up too! The dough is really easy to work with.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Sara"},"datePublished":"2022-04-08"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"I have had a similar version of these many years ago...I served mine with sliced fresh tomato &amp; rocket rolled up in each slice with the lemon juice and the kids inhaled them and begged for more!\r\nAbsolutely fantastic recipe - even for fuss pots!","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Natalie"},"datePublished":"2022-04-04"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Wonderful!! Easy instructions to follow. Better than any Turkish restaurant I have had. And its homemade!","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Barbara"},"datePublished":"2022-04-03"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"I loved these! Perfect in every way. I mixed more dough because we had more meat mixture.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Christina"},"datePublished":"2022-04-02"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"I've made this a few time and I love it! Thanks for sharing this recipe with us.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Manny"},"datePublished":"2022-03-25"}],"recipeCategory":["Appetizer","Main Course","Snack"],"recipeCuisine":["Mediterranean","Middle Eastern","Turkish"],"suitableForDiet":["https:\/\/schema.org\/LowLactoseDiet"],"keywords":"Flatbread, Traditional Turkish Recipes, Turkish pizza","nutrition":{"@type":"NutritionInformation","calories":"411 kcal","carbohydrateContent":"51 g","proteinContent":"17 g","fatContent":"15 g","saturatedFatContent":"5 g","transFatContent":"1 g","cholesterolContent":"41 mg","sodiumContent":"1044 mg","fiberContent":"4 g","sugarContent":"5 g","unsaturatedFatContent":"8 g","servingSize":"1 serving"},"@id":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#recipe","isPartOf":{"@id":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/#article"},"mainEntityOfPage":"https:\/\/cookingorgeous.com\/blog\/homemade-turkish-lahmacun\/"}]}</script>
