</style><details id="feast-advanced-jump-to"open><summary>Jump to:</summary><ul id="feast-jump-to-list"><li><a href="#what-is-lahmacun">What Is Lahmacun? </a></li><li><a href="#ingredients-youll-need">Ingredients You&#039;ll Need</a></li><li><a href="#how-to-make-homemade-lahmacun">How to Make Homemade Lahmacun?</a></li><li><a href="#lahmacun-vs-pide">Lahmacun vs Pide </a></li><li><a href="#why-this-recipe-works">Why This Recipe Works?</a></li><li><a href="#how-to-eat-turkish-lahmacun">How to Eat Turkish Lahmacun?</a></li><li><a href="#top-tips-from-the-chef">Top Tips From the Chef</a></li><li><a href="#recipe-faqs">Recipe FAQs</a></li><li><a href="#related-recipes">Related Recipes</a></li><li><a href="#turkish-lahmacun">Turkish Lahmacun</a></li></ul></details>


<p>Lahmacun (or Lahmajoun) wrap made with fresh parsley leaves, a few slices of red onions, and a squeeze of fresh lemon juice served with a glass of <a href="https://cookingorgeous.com/blog/ayran-turkish-yogurt-drink/">Ayran (Turkish Yogurt Drink)</a> is the perfect lunchtime snack! </p>



<p>If you love street food, you may also want to take a look at my other recipes, such as <a href="https://cookingorgeous.com/blog/izmir-kumru-turkish-sandwich/">Izmir Kumru - Turkish Sandwich,</a> <a href="https://cookingorgeous.com/blog/thai-chicken-satay-with-peanut-sauce/">Thai Chicken Satay with Peanut Sauce</a>, and <a href="https://cookingorgeous.com/blog/tantuni/">Tantuni</a>.</p>



<div class="adthrive-video-player in-post" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/VideoObject" data-video-id="lojVxLyy" data-player-type="default" override-embed="default">
			<meta itemprop="uploadDate" content="2023-01-06T00:00:00+00:00" />
		<meta itemprop="name" content="Turkish Lahmacun (Lahmajun)" />
		<meta itemprop="description" content="Homemade Turkish Lahmacun (or Lahmajun-Lahmajoun) is a super-thin crispy flatbread topped with minced beef or lamb mixed with vegetables, herbs, and spices. You can find this popular street / fast food everywhere in Turkey, in restaurants, cafes, and fast-food shops." />
		<meta itemprop="thumbnailUrl" content="https://content.jwplatform.com/thumbs/lojVxLyy-720.jpg" />
		<meta itemprop="contentUrl" content="https://content.jwplatform.com/videos/lojVxLyy.mp4" />
	</div>




<h2 id="what-is-lahmacun"   class="wp-block-heading">What Is Lahmacun? </h2>



<p>Lahmacun - pronounced as lah-ma-jun (lah-ma-Joon) is a popular Turkish and Middle Eastern dish that can be described as <em><strong><a href="https://cookingorgeous.com/blog/turkish-pide-bread-ramazan-pidesi/">flatbread</a>&nbsp;with spicy ground meat</strong></em> or <strong><em>flatbread pizza.</em></strong></p>



<p>This super thin crispy flatbread is topped with a delicious filling made of ground lamb (or beef), finely chopped vegetables, and a variety of spices and herbs. The dough is then baked in a very hot oven until it is crispy and slightly charred around the edges.</p>



<p>Just like <a href="https://cookingorgeous.com/blog/arayes-meat-stuffed-pita/">Arayes (Meat Stuffed Pita)</a>, this <strong><em>flatbread pizza</em></strong> is also commonly enjoyed as a snack or appetiser, with a side of yogurt sauce or a salad on the side. Lahmacun is similar to <a href="https://cookingorgeous.com/blog/pide-turkish-kiymali-pide/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Kiymali Turkish Pide</a>, but the dough is thinner and is shaped round instead of a boat shape.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%20800'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="lahmacun wrapped with parsley and tomatoes" class="wp-image-35134" data-lazy-srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-28.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-28-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-28-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-28-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-28-150x100.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-28.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-28.jpg" alt="lahmacun wrapped with parsley and tomatoes" class="wp-image-35134" srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-28.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-28-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-28-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-28-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-28-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<p>Even though there is no clear evidence about where it was invented, they are popular in countries formerly parts of the Ottoman Empire, especially Turkey, Lebanon, Armenia, Syria, and Iraq.&nbsp;</p>



<p>Lahmacun is often called "<em>Turkish pizza</em>", "<em>Turkish Lamb Pizza</em>", " <em>Flatbread Pizza</em>", or "<em>Lahmacun pizza</em>" in Western countries. </p>



<h2 id="ingredients-youll-need"   class="wp-block-heading">Ingredients You'll Need</h2>



<p><em>Please scroll down to the recipe card below for the&nbsp;full ingredients list with&nbsp;measurements, complete recipe method, recipe notes, and nutritional information.</em></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Lahmacun Dough</h3>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="960" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%20960'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Labelled picture of ingredients for lahmacun dough" class="wp-image-28455" data-lazy-srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-30.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-30-300x240.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-30-1024x819.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-30-768x614.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-30-150x120.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-30.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="960" src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-30.jpg" alt="Labelled picture of ingredients for lahmacun dough" class="wp-image-28455" srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-30.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-30-300x240.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-30-1024x819.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-30-768x614.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-30-150x120.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Strong white flour</strong> / <strong>strong&nbsp;bread&nbsp;flour</strong> -  <em>It gives some elasticity to the dough which makes it easier to roll out.</em></li>
</ul>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Olive oil</strong> - It tenderizes and flavors the lahmacun dough, while also creating a crispy texture on the bottom.</li>
</ul>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Meat Filling</h3>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="960" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%20960'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Labelled picture of ingredients for lahmacun filling" class="wp-image-28457" data-lazy-srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-31.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-31-300x240.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-31-1024x819.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-31-768x614.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-31-150x120.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-31.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="960" src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-31.jpg" alt="Labelled picture of ingredients for lahmacun filling" class="wp-image-28457" srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-31.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-31-300x240.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-31-1024x819.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-31-768x614.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-31-150x120.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Ground beef or lamb </strong>- You can use beef or lamb, or a mixture of both. Try and use fatty meat, with a minimum of 15-20% fat. Ground lamb is naturally fatty, but if using beef or a mixture, make sure your ground beef isn’t lean. <em>If you only have lean beef, add a tablespoon of olive oil to your filling to help it stick to the dough.</em></li>
</ul>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Turkish green peppers&nbsp;</strong>- Always check the spiciness before using them and don't use any extra chili or chili flakes if you don't want overly hot lahmacuns. You can replace them with bell pepper or Spanish Padron peppers.</li>
</ul>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong><strong><strong>Tomato paste</strong> <strong>-</strong></strong></strong> It is the staple of Turkish cooking. It adds an umami flavor to the dishes as well as a bright red color. You can find it in Turkish or Middle Eastern shops. You can also buy it from <span data-eafl-id="12619" data-eafl-parsed="1" class="eafl-link eafl-link-html" style="display: inline-block;"><a target="_blank" href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B00B0GJ13A/ref=as_li_tl?ie=UTF8&camp=1789&creative=9325&creativeASIN=B00B0GJ13A&linkCode=as2&tag=cookingorgeou-20&linkId=9e95d043c963d74dfb5ba30064fc3c37">Amazon </a></span>. </li>
</ul>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Red pepper paste - </strong>Turkish red pepper paste is a rich, delicious paste made with juicy, spicy red peppers and I use it quite often in my Turkish recipes. You can buy it from Turkish or Middle Eastern shops. You can also buy it from <span data-eafl-id="12579" data-eafl-parsed="1" class="eafl-link eafl-link-html" style="display: inline-block;"><a target="_blank" href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B00VOBJNZW/ref=as_li_tl?ie=UTF8&camp=1789&creative=9325&creativeASIN=B00VOBJNZW&linkCode=as2&tag=cookingorgeou-20&linkId=932aa5555e1e2512fbd9dc2c829fc595">Amazon </a></span>. Alternatively, you can omit it and use the same amount of tomato paste.</li>
</ul>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Parsley </strong>- Use fresh flatleaf parsley for both the lahmacun filling and for lahmacun wraps.</li>
</ul>



<h2 id="how-to-make-homemade-lahmacun"   class="wp-block-heading">How to Make Homemade Lahmacun?</h2>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Prepare the Dough</strong></h3>



<p>This simple dough needs only 4 ingredients, and yeast is not one of them! If you don't feel confident working with yeast, this is the perfect recipe for you.</p>



<p>To make the dough, place the water, olive oil, and salt in a bowl and then mix them until combined. </p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%20800'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="flour, water, salt and olive oil are placed in a bowl" class="wp-image-28458" data-lazy-srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-32.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-32-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-32-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-32-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-32-150x100.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-32.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-32.jpg" alt="flour, water, salt and olive oil are placed in a bowl" class="wp-image-28458" srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-32.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-32-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-32-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-32-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-32-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<p>Use a stand mixer if you prefer. Sift the flour, add gradually to the bowl, and then knead the dough. Use the dough hook if you are using your stand mixer.</p>



<p>Add enough flour to have&nbsp;the dough come together and then form a soft and slightly sticky dough.&nbsp;Knead the dough for 5-6 minutes, until it is elastic, smooth, and not sticky anymore.&nbsp;</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%20800'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="lahmacun dough in a glass bowl" class="wp-image-28459" data-lazy-srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-33.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-33-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-33-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-33-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-33-150x100.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-33.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-33.jpg" alt="lahmacun dough in a glass bowl" class="wp-image-28459" srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-33.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-33-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-33-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-33-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-33-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<p>Once the dough is smooth, divide it into 6 balls (approximately 3 oz/90 grams each) and place them on a lightly floured tray or worktop. </p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="817" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%20817'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Divide the dough into 6 equal pieces" class="wp-image-8699" data-lazy-srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-5.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-5-300x204.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-5-1024x697.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-5-768x523.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-5-150x102.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-5.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="817" src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-5.jpg" alt="Divide the dough into 6 equal pieces" class="wp-image-8699" srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-5.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-5-300x204.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-5-1024x697.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-5-768x523.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-5-150x102.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<p>Cover the dough balls with a clean kitchen towel or cling film and let them rest at room temperature for about 20 minutes. <em>This step is necessary for the dough to relax and makes it easier to roll out.&nbsp;</em>Prepare the lahmacun filling while the dough is resting.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Prepare the Fillin</strong>g</h3>



<p>Place onion, peppers (both green and red), tomatoes, garlic, and chili (if using fresh) in a food processor. </p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%20800'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="place the vegetables into a food processor" class="wp-image-8700" data-lazy-srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-6.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-6-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-6-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-6-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-6-150x100.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-6.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-6.jpg" alt="place the vegetables into a food processor" class="wp-image-8700" srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-6.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-6-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-6-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-6-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-6-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<p>Finely chop them using the pulse function. <em>Be careful at this stage not to turn them into purée.</em> Alternatively, you can finely chop them using a sharp knife.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%20800'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="vegetables are blitzed in a food processo" class="wp-image-8701" data-lazy-srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-7.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-7-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-7-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-7-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-7-150x100.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-7.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-7.jpg" alt="vegetables are blitzed in a food processo" class="wp-image-8701" srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-7.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-7-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-7-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-7-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-7-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<p>Transfer the vegetables to a bowl and add the ground meat, tomato paste, pepper paste, finely chopped parsley, freshly ground black pepper, paprika, and salt.</p>



<p>You can replace red pepper paste with tomato paste if you don't have it in your fridge, or make your own with my <a href="https://cookingorgeous.com/blog/biber-salcasi-turkish-red-pepper-paste/">simple biber salcasi recipe</a>.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%20800'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="mix the chopped vegetables with minced meat and spices" class="wp-image-8702" data-lazy-srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-8.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-8-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-8-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-8-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-8-150x100.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-8.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-8.jpg" alt="mix the chopped vegetables with minced meat and spices" class="wp-image-8702" srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-8.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-8-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-8-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-8-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-8-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<p>Mix well until all combined into a smooth mixture that is easy to spread.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Start Cooking Lahmacun on a Pan</h3>



<p>The traditional way to cook the lahmacun is in a wood oven. But it is still possible to make delicious lahmacuns at home in a domestic oven combined with a stovetop.</p>



<p>Preheat the oven to 450° F (230° C) and then line a large sheet tray with parchment paper. Set it aside. Heat a large non-stick pan with a lid over medium-high heat. Ideally, the pan should be 10" (26 cm)Ø or bigger.</p>



<p>Roll out a dough ball into a thin circle size of 9 ½" (25 cm) Ø. If your pan is smaller than that, roll the dough ball small enough to fit in it.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%20800'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="roll a dough ball out size of 25 cm dia" class="wp-image-8703" data-lazy-srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-9.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-9-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-9-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-9-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-9-150x100.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-9.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-9.jpg" alt="roll a dough ball out size of 25 cm dia" class="wp-image-8703" srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-9.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-9-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-9-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-9-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-9-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<p>Place the dough circle in the hot pan. Divide your mixture into 6 and then spread ⅙ of the mixture on a dough circle evenly and thinly, including the edges. <em>Gently press the filling into the dough to ensure it sticks. </em></p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1125" height="802" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201125%20802'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Homemade Turkish lahmacun cooking on a pan" class="wp-image-8853" data-lazy-srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-17.jpg 1125w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-17-300x214.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-17-1024x730.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-17-768x547.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-17-150x107.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1125px) 100vw, 1125px" data-lazy-src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-17.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1125" height="802" src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-17.jpg" alt="Homemade Turkish lahmacun cooking on a pan" class="wp-image-8853" srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-17.jpg 1125w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-17-300x214.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-17-1024x730.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-17-768x547.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-17-150x107.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1125px) 100vw, 1125px" /></noscript></figure>



<p>Cook it for 4-5 minutes or until you see some brown spots at the bottom. </p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Finish Baking in the Oven</h3>



<p>Transfer the lahmacun to your prepared baking sheet. Bake them in the preheated oven for 5 to 7 minutes or until they are crispy on the outside and the filling is thoroughly cooked.&nbsp;Transfer them to a large plate and then cover them with tin foil or a clean kitchen towel while the rest of the lahmacuns are baking.</p>



<p>You can prepare the second dough ball while the first one is baking. Repeat with the remaining dough balls and filling. <em>Covering them will help to keep the lahmacuns warm, and it will soften them enough for you to be able to roll them into wraps.</em></p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%20800'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="" class="wp-image-35135" data-lazy-srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-29.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-29-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-29-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-29-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-29-150x100.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-29.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-29.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-35135" srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-29.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-29-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-29-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-29-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-29-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<h2 id="lahmacun-vs-pide"   class="wp-block-heading">Lahmacun vs Pide </h2>



<p>Lahmacun and pide are both Turkish dishes, but they have some differences.</p>



<p>Pide is usually topped with different toppings such as<strong> <a href="https://cookingorgeous.com/blog/pide-with-cheese-and-mushrooms/">mushroom and cheese,</a> <a href="https://cookingorgeous.com/blog/sucuklu-pide/">sucuk</a> </strong>(a type of Turkish spicy sausage), or a <strong><a href="https://cookingorgeous.com/blog/pide-turkish-kiymali-pide/">mix of beef and vegetables</a>.</strong> <em>Lahmacun is made with minced beef mixed with onions, peppers,</em> and tomatoes.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1200" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%201200'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="cooked lahmacun are stacked together to keep them warm" class="wp-image-8856" data-lazy-srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18-300x300.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18-150x150.jpg 150w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18-768x768.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18-500x500.jpg 500w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18-360x361.jpg 360w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18-96x96.jpg 96w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1200" src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18.jpg" alt="cooked lahmacun are stacked together to keep them warm" class="wp-image-8856" srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18-300x300.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18-150x150.jpg 150w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18-768x768.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18-500x500.jpg 500w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18-360x361.jpg 360w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-18-96x96.jpg 96w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<p><em>Lahmacun is very thin, round-shaped, and is often eaten like a wrap</em>.&nbsp;The pide<strong> is boat-shaped and has a thicker crust.</strong> While both lahmacun and pide are popular Turkish dishes, they are distinct from each other in terms of their texture, toppings, and how they are served.</p>



<h2 id="why-this-recipe-works"   class="wp-block-heading">Why This Recipe Works?</h2>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>It is easy to make Homemade Turkish Lahmacun with step-by-step instructions and the video attached to the recipe card. </li>
</ul>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><em>You can make this famous street food in your kitchen without needing a wood ov</em>en.</li>
</ul>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Lahmacun <strong>(or Lahmajun-Lahmajoun)</strong> is made with a very simple non-yeast dough.</li>
</ul>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>You can serve this <strong><em>flatbread pizza</em></strong> for dinner as a main course or you can make it smaller and serve it as an appetizer. </li>
</ul>



<h2 id="how-to-eat-turkish-lahmacun"   class="wp-block-heading">How to Eat Turkish Lahmacun?</h2>



<p>Lahmacun is not only a snack, but it is also perfect to serve as a meal for lunch, dinner, or as an appetizer. The typical way to enjoy it is by topping it with fresh parsley leaves, red onion, tomato, and cucumber slices.</p>



<p>You can add a generous squeeze of lemon juice to enhance the flavors. To complement the dish, make sure to have a glass of refreshing <a href="https://cookingorgeous.com/blog/ayran-turkish-yogurt-drink/">Turkish Yogurt Drink - Ayran</a>! You can either eat it wrapped with a salad like a burrito or slice it like a pizza.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%20800'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="6 pieces of lahmacun" class="wp-image-35133" data-lazy-srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-25.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-25-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-25-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-25-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-25-150x100.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-25.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" src="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-25.jpg" alt="6 pieces of lahmacun" class="wp-image-35133" srcset="https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-25.jpg 1200w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-25-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-25-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-25-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cookingorgeous.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/homemade-turkish-lahmacun-recipe-25-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<p>I also quite like to add a good pinch of flaked chili (pul biber) on top of my Lahmacun.</p>



<p>If you want to serve Lahmacun as a meal, it is best to serve it with a bowl of soup such as <a href="https://cookingorgeous.com/blog/turkish-lentil-soup/">Turkish Lentil Soup</a>, <a href="https://cookingorgeous.com/blog/red-pepper-and-tomato-soup/">Red Pepper and Tomato Soup</a>, or <a href="https://cookingorgeous.com/blog/ezogelin-soup/">Ezogelin Corbasi.</a></p>



<h2 id="top-tips-from-the-chef"   class="wp-block-heading">Top Tips From the Chef</h2>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Use minced meat with a high percentage of fat for topping. It will not only improve the taste but also will make the filling easy to spread on the dough.</li>
</ul>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Knead the dough minimum for 5 minutes until it feels elastic and soft. When you have an elastic dough, you can shape it easily without tearing it.</li>
</ul>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Let the dough balls rest at room temperature for about 20 minutes. <em>This step is necessary for the dough to relax and makes it easier to roll out.&nbsp;</em></li>
</ul>



<h2 id="recipe-faqs"   class="wp-block-heading">Recipe FAQs</h2>



<div class="schema-faq wp-block-yoast-faq-block"><div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1635521908574"><strong class="schema-faq-question">Is Lahmacun healthy?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">Lahmacun is considered healthy, it has a moderate amount of calories (411 calories per lahmacun with my recipe) and it is a good source of Vitamin A, Vitamin C, and Manganese. It is also considered a good source of protein.<br/></p> </div> <div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1661691506361"><strong class="schema-faq-question">Can you freeze the leftovers?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">Yes, the leftovers can be frozen and kept in the freezer for up to 3 months. Make sure you cool them down totally and wrap them individually before freezing them.</p> </div> <div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1661691545245"><strong class="schema-faq-question">Can you prepare lahmacun in advance?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">You can make the mince filling up to 3 days in advance and keep it refrigerated in an airtight container until you need it. <br/>The same goes for the dough. Make sure to bring the dough to room temperature before dividing and rolling them out.</p> </div> </div>



